Lodestone bundles and distributes the following third-party components. Each is
listed with its licence, the upstream project it comes from, and — where we had
to modify it to run on Android — the fork carrying those changes.

Every fork below sits on the exact upstream commit its released binary was built
from, with our patches as individual commits on the `lodestone/android-arm64`
branch, so the published source corresponds to the published binary.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenJDK  (java 8, 17, 21, 25)
    GPL-2.0 WITH Classpath-exception-2.0
    https://github.com/openjdk/jdk8u   -> https://github.com/lodestone-launcher/jdk8u
    https://github.com/openjdk/jdk17u  -> https://github.com/lodestone-launcher/jdk17u
    https://github.com/openjdk/jdk21u  -> https://github.com/lodestone-launcher/jdk21u
    https://github.com/openjdk/jdk25u  -> https://github.com/lodestone-launcher/jdk25u

    Modified. The Classpath exception is what allows Lodestone's own code to
    remain separately licensed while linking against the runtime; the runtime
    itself stays GPL, and its corresponding source is the tagged branch above.

OpenAL Soft
    LGPL-2.1-or-later
    https://github.com/kcat/openal-soft, tag 1.23.1, commit d3875f333

    Unmodified. Cross-compiled for Android from that exact commit with no source
    changes, so upstream is the corresponding source. It ships as a separate
    shared library and is loaded dynamically, so it may be replaced with another
    build of the same version.

Mesa  (Zink, and the libdrm it builds against)
    MIT
    https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa
    -> https://github.com/lodestone-launcher/mesa

    Modified. Four patches, none of them driver-specific: three teach an
    Android build to export and bind the desktop GL entry points and to
    connect a native window when EGL is loaded directly, and one lets Zink be
    pointed at a chosen Vulkan library. Zink runs on the device's own
    libvulkan.so; no Vulkan driver is built or shipped.

gl4es
    MIT
    https://github.com/ptitSeb/gl4es

    Unmodified. Built from the upstream default branch; see runtime/build-gl4es.sh.

LWJGL 3.3.3 and 3.4.1  (and their vendored stb, tinyfiledialogs and
Vulkan Memory Allocator)
    BSD-3-Clause
    https://github.com/LWJGL/lwjgl3

    Unmodified where it stands on its own. Cross-compiled for Android; see
    runtime/build-lwjgl.sh.

    Repackaged for the LWJGL 2 compatibility layer, which redistributes the
    core, GLFW and OpenGL modules inside one jar. The OpenGL module's classes
    are moved to com.github.lodestone.lwjgl3.opengl and its JNI symbols renamed
    to match, because the layer has to declare org.lwjgl.opengl itself and the
    two would otherwise collide. No source is otherwise changed; the rename is
    applied by build-lwjgl.sh and by the relocation task in app/build.gradle.kts,
    both of which are mechanical and reproducible from the upstream tag.

LWJGL 2.9.4
    BSD-3-Clause
    https://github.com/LWJGL/lwjgl

    Not distributed. Its jar is read at development time by
    runtime/generate-lwjgl2-bindings.py, which takes the class names, method
    signatures and constant values the compatibility layer is obliged to declare
    so that a game compiled against LWJGL 2 links against it. The generated
    bodies are ours and forward to LWJGL 3; nothing is copied from LWJGL 2's
    implementation.

FreeType
    FTL  (dual-licensed FTL / GPL-2.0; Lodestone takes the FTL)
    https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype

    Unmodified. Portions of this software are copyright (c) The FreeType Project
    (www.freetype.org). All rights reserved.

libffi
    MIT
    https://github.com/libffi/libffi

    Unmodified. Linked into LWJGL's core native library.

shaderc  (with glslang and SPIRV-Tools, which it builds in)
    Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/google/shaderc, tag v2025.2

    Unmodified. Cross-compiled for Android from that tag; see
    runtime/build-lwjgl.sh. Minecraft's Vulkan backend compiles its GLSL to
    SPIR-V through it at run time.

SPIRV-Cross
    Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Cross, tag vulkan-sdk-1.3.290.0

    Unmodified. Cross-compiled for Android; the Vulkan backend reflects its
    compiled SPIR-V through the C API to find each shader's uniforms and
    samplers.

Vulkan Memory Allocator
    MIT
    https://github.com/GPUOpen-LibrariesAndSDKs/VulkanMemoryAllocator

    Unmodified. Header-only, vendored by LWJGL and compiled into
    liblwjgl_vma.so from LWJGL's own generated bindings.

LLVM libc++  (libc++_shared.so)
    Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
    https://llvm.org

    Unmodified, as shipped in the Android NDK.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vulkan itself is not distributed. It is a system library on every device
Lodestone installs on, and the launcher points LWJGL at Android's own
libvulkan.so rather than shipping a loader.

